Notes
-------------------------------------------------------------------

GitHub's automatic licence detector will likely read this file as MIT
and label the whole repository accordingly. That label is a convenience,
not a legal statement. Section 2 governs the brand assets regardless of
what the sidebar says.

This file was drafted for a small open-source project and is not legal
advice. If Phantaslate ever needs enforceable trademark protection —
registration, or defending the name commercially — that is worth a
conversation with an actual lawyer rather than a text file.
